course: dictionary
lesson: 6794
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The verb ordain is a good example. In church, «Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain only men as priests» means they make people into priests in a special ceremony. Look at the words around it: church and priests are your clues.
explain: Outside church, ordain means to order or decide something officially. «A king may ordain a new law» means the king makes the law official. Ask yourself: is this about church, or about a king, a law or an official decision? The sentence will show you.
explain: Ordain can also mean that something was decided in advance, as if by God or fate. «It was ordained that they would meet» means it was meant to happen. Try swapping in decide: the sentence still makes sense, but it sounds planned, as if it was always going to happen.
fact: «Ordain» is a verb: ordain, ordains, ordained, ordaining.
fact: In church, to ordain someone is to make them a priest, minister or rabbi in a special religious ceremony.
fact: To ordain something can mean to order or decide it officially, as a king or law does.
fact: «Ordained» can mean decided in advance by God or fate, as in «It was ordained that they would meet».
fact: Churches do not all agree: Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain only men as priests, while many Protestant and Anglican churches have women ministers and bishops.
exercise: «Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain only men as priests.» What does ordain mean here? | To run away from danger | To sing loudly in a choir | To paint a picture of a priest | *To make someone into a priest
exercise: «A king may ordain a new law.» What does ordain mean in this sentence? | To read a law quietly | To break a law | To lose a law | *To order or decide a law officially
exercise: «It was ordained that they would meet.» What does this suggest? | *It was decided in advance, as if by fate | They argued about meeting | They met by accident, with no plan | They never met at all
test: Which word means to make someone a priest in a special religious ceremony? | *ordain | hide | paint | forgive
test: Churches disagree about who can be ordained. What does this tell you? | *Christians read the Bible differently, so they do not all agree | Priests are never ordained | Everyone agrees about everything in the Bible | Bibles are all exactly the same
exam: In «divinely ordained», the word divinely means from God. So ordained most likely means | bought from a shop | painted in bright colours | *decided by God or fate | lost for ever
